### What happened?

When adding `eval "$(atuin pty-proxy init bash)"` to the top of my bashrc, my umask gets changed to `0077`, instead of the `0002` it is set to by PAM. This keeps catching me out and causing issues, e.g. taking down my Mastodon web interface, because after running an upgrade the www-data user had no access to read the precompiled asset files. I've tested this on both bash and zsh, across multiple Ubuntu machines, and a single Rocky Linux server; and get the same outcome. I've added a screen recording showing that adding or removing this line is what causes umask to change.

I don't *believe* this is intentional, but if it is, it should be documented somewhere.

